## 1. License for Non-Commercial Use

Subject to compliance with this Agreement, the Licensor grants, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of the Software a non-exclusive license to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, and distribute the Software and modified versions thereof solely for non-commercial purposes.

“Non-commercial purposes” means use that is not intended to obtain commercial benefits or monetary compensation and does not serve for-profit business activities, such as personal learning, research, testing, and exchanges that meet these conditions.

Whether a user is an individual, a business, or a non-profit organization does not, by itself, determine the nature of the use; the determination must be based on the actual purpose of the use.

## 2. Paid Authorization Required for Commercial Use

Any commercial use requires a separate, valid commercial license from the Licensor before such use begins, and payment of the license fees in accordance with the parties’ agreement.

“Commercial use” means use intended to obtain commercial benefits or monetary compensation, or to serve for-profit business activities, including, without limitation:

1. Selling, renting, or otherwise providing the Software or modified versions thereof for a fee.
2. Integrating the Software into commercial products, paid services, subscription services, or services that generate commercial revenue, such as advertising revenue.
3. Using the Software for internal business operations, commercial production, client projects, or other for-profit business activities.
4. Using the Software to create, generate, or process novels, copywriting, or other content intended for publication and sale, paid reading access, advertising monetization, or delivery as part of a commercial engagement.

Providing products, services, or content to end users free of charge does not, by itself, constitute non-commercial use; the determination must still be based on the actual purpose of the use and its commercial revenue model.

## 3. Scope of Commercial Authorization

The licensee, permitted purposes, covered versions, scope of use, term, fees, and payment method of a commercial license shall be governed by the written or electronic commercial license agreement confirmed by both parties.

Obtaining a license for commercial use does not automatically grant the right to resell the Software, sublicense it, distribute it commercially, or provide the Software to third parties as a service. Such rights must be expressly set out in the commercial license agreement.

If a commercial license agreement conflicts with this Agreement, the commercial license agreement shall prevail within the scope it expressly authorizes.

